		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A lone function-expression argument takes three states: hugged flat, hugged with the",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 107
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " function's own group broken, then the argument on its own line. The middle state exists",
			"start": 109,
			"end": 199
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " only when the signature has something to break - a parameter list of plain identifiers",
			"start": 201,
			"end": 290
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " renders flat inside the hug, so it drops to the last state instead.",
			"start": 292,
			"end": 362
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " Boundary: exactly 100 chars - fits, the function stays hugged.",
			"start": 365,
			"end": 430
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " Boundary: exactly 101 chars - nothing inside can break, so the argument takes its own line.",
			"start": 533,
			"end": 627
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The `new` twin takes the same three states.",
			"start": 736,
			"end": 782
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A body of its own forces the break, so the function stays hugged past width.",
			"start": 891,
			"end": 970
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " Plain identifier parameters render flat inside the hug, so an over-wide list cannot break",
